  * feat(client): enable pty-proxy via config (#3828)
   - Adds a `[pty_proxy] enabled` config setting. When set, `atuin init`
   - emits the pty-proxy exec preamble first, so the proxy starts without a
   - separate `atuin pty-proxy init` line in shell config.
   - - Guarded by `ATUIN_PTY_PROXY_ACTIVE`, so we won't get nested sessions
   - - Unsupported shells (xonsh, powershell) or builds without pty-proxy
   - warn on stderr instead of emitting shell code
   - - Docs updated to present the config option as the primary method
  * chore: Richer logging for atuin-server (#2564)
