  * fix: Close OSC133 C when launching Atuin AI to prevent content erasure (#3794)
  * ci: run CodSpeed walltime benchmarks on depot-macos-26 (#3791)
   - The shared `codspeed-macro` pool has been queueing PR benchmark runs for
   - 20+ minutes, and CodSpeed flags its comparisons with "different runtime
   - environments detected" — the base and head runs land on different runner
   - generations, which makes small regressions/improvements hard to trust
   - (see the noise on #3782).
   - Depot's macOS runners are whole dedicated machines, so walltime numbers
   - should be stable and comparable run to run. CodSpeed's runner ships
   - `aarch64-apple-darwin` builds, so walltime mode is supported there.
   - Merging this first lets `main` record baseline benchmark data on the new
   - runner; #3782 will then rebase and re-benchmark against a like-for-like
   - base.
