  * bench: daemon search benchmark (divan + CodSpeed) (#3763)
   - Benchmarks + CI only — no behavior changes. Merging this first records
   - the nucleo-era baseline on CodSpeed, so the frizbee PR stacked on top
   - (#3782) shows its improvement directly in its CodSpeed report.
   - ## What
   - Adds `crates/atuin-search-bench`: a
   - [divan](https://github.com/nvzqz/divan) benchmark measuring the daemon's
   - `SearchIndex::search` **end-to-end** — index built from
   - shell-history-shaped data, then queried the way the interactive UI does
   - (realistic query set, limit 200, including the empty-query and
   - directory-filtered paths).
   - - **Engine-agnostic benchmark names**
   - (`daemon_search[<scale>/<query>]`): they measure whatever fuzzy matcher
   - the daemon currently uses, so an engine swap shows up as a step change
   - in the tracked series rather than as a new set of benchmarks.
   - - Deterministic synthetic history generator shaped after a real
   - 168k-line history (zipf-ish repeated head, templated body with
   - high-cardinality args so uniqueness lands near real history's ~30%, long
   - tail incl. very long commands and some unicode). `BENCH_DATA` runs
   - against a real exported history instead; `BENCH_SCALES`/`BENCH_SEED` env
   - knobs, sampling tuned via divan's own `DIVAN_*` vars.
   - - Result counts are sanity-checked per scale so a broken query or filter
   - shows up in the logs rather than as a suspiciously fast run.
   - - The `divan` dependency is CodSpeed's drop-in compat crate, so the same
   - bench runs natively via `cargo bench` and instrumented under
   - `cargo-codspeed`.
   - - CI: wired into the existing `codspeed.yml` workflow (adds `-p
   - atuin-search-bench` to the build/run, with a reduced `BENCH_SCALES`
   - since instrumented index builds at 1M+ lines would dominate the job).
   - ## Baseline this records (M-series MacBook, native, 1M history lines /
   - 188k unique commands)
   - | query | current daemon (nucleo) |
   - |---|---|
   - | empty | 9.1 ms |
   - | `git` | 18.5 ms |
   - | `git p` | 19.2 ms |
   - | `docker compose up` | 20.5 ms |
   - | `zzznomatchzzz` | 16.9 ms |
   - | `git` (directory filter) | 39.0 ms |
   - #3782 drops these 69–95%.
  * Add CodSpeed continuous benchmarking (#3784)
   - This wires the existing `divan` benchmarks up to CodSpeed so that
   - performance is measured on every push to `main` and on every pull
   - request, and extends the benchmark coverage of a few hot paths.
   - ## What changed
   - **CodSpeed integration**
   - - `divan` is now the
   - [`codspeed-divan-compat`](https://codspeed.io/docs/benchmarks/rust/divan)
   - crate (renamed to `divan`) in `atuin-client`, `atuin-history` and
   - `atuin-nucleo-matcher`. Imports and benchmark code are unchanged, and
   - the layer is a passthrough outside of `cargo codspeed`, so plain `cargo
   - bench` keeps working exactly as before.
   - - New `.github/workflows/codspeed.yml` builds the benchmark targets with
   - `cargo codspeed build` and runs them through `CodSpeedHQ/action@v4` in
   - `simulation` mode (deterministic CPU simulation, hardware agnostic, with
   - flamegraphs). It runs on `depot-ubuntu-24.04`, like the rest of the Rust
   - CI, authenticates via OIDC, and supports `workflow_dispatch` so CodSpeed
   - can backfill historical data.
   - - CodSpeed badge added to the README, and the benchmark section of
   - `AGENTS.md` updated.
   - **New benchmarks**
   - - `atuin-client`: `history_store.rs` covers
   - `HistoryRecord::{serialize,deserialize}` for a single entry and for a
   - 100 entry sync page. Every recorded command is serialized before being
   - stored or synced, and every entry pulled from the server is deserialized
   - again.
   - - `atuin-client`: `record/encryption.rs` covers PASETO V4 envelope
   - `encrypt`/`decrypt` of history records, which runs once per synced
   - entry.
   - - `atuin-nucleo-matcher`: `fuzzy_match.rs` covers `Matcher::fuzzy_match`
   - over 200/1000/10000 candidates and `Pattern::match_list` for the four
   - atom kinds a user can type (fuzzy, multi word, `'substring`, `^prefix`).
   - This is re-run on every keystroke in the search UI, so it is the most
   - latency-sensitive code in the client. The corpus is generated
   - deterministically from a fixed seed, with no external crate, instead of
   - relying on a checkout of the Linux tree like the existing `brunch` bench
   - does.
   - **Existing benchmark made reproducible**
   - - `atuin-history/benches/smart_sort.rs` generated its history inside the
   - measured closure using `rand::thread_rng()` and
   - `OffsetDateTime::now_utc()`. Generation now happens in `with_inputs`
   - (excluded from measurement) with a seeded RNG and a fixed "now",
   - matching the `BenchCtx` pattern already used in `atuin-client`. Without
   - this, most of the measurement was history generation and results were
   - not reproducible.
   - ## Local verification
   - `codspeed run --mode simulation -- cargo codspeed run` measured all 27
   - benchmarks:
   - - `atuin-client`: `serialize`, `deserialize`, `encrypt`, `decrypt` (1,
   - 100), `reorder_fuzzy_bench` (10, 200, 1000), `push_batch` (1, 10, 100)
   - - `atuin-history`: `smart_sort` (100 to 10000)
   - - `atuin-nucleo-matcher`: `fuzzy_match` (200, 1000, 10000), `match_list`
   - (4 query shapes)
   - `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --benches` are clean, and `cargo
   - bench` still runs the suites with the stock divan output.
   - ## Next steps
   - - Merge this PR to get a baseline on `main`; subsequent PRs will then be
   - annotated with a performance report.
   - - `push_batch` spends most of its time in SQLite syscalls, which the
   - simulation instrument reports separately as system time. If you want
   - that path tracked as wall time instead, it can be moved to a `walltime`
   - job on CodSpeed macro runners.
   - - The `atuin-nucleo-bench` binary (brunch, requires cloning the Linux
   - tree) is left untouched; the new matcher benchmark covers the same code
   - path in CI without the external checkout.
   - Co-authored-by: CodSpeed Bot <no-reply@codspeed.io>
  * chore: Remove Store trait (#3779)
  * chore(ci): fix `package` step (#3770)
   - Right now, the CI `package` step sometimes pulls the `atuin*` crates
   - from crates.io instead of the local tree. This PR fixes that by clearing
   - the relevant cached artifacts. Compared to the approach of reducing the
   - cached paths (removing `target` and `~/.cargo/registry/src`), this
   - approach builds much faster as all of the non-Atuin dependencies don't
   - have to be compiled every time.
  * docs: clarify update check network, provide build command (#3767)
   - <!-- Thank you for making a PR! Bug fixes are always welcome, but if
   - you're adding a new feature or changing an existing one, we'd really
   - appreciate if you open an issue, post on the forum, or drop in on
   - Discord -->
   - ## Checks
   - - [ ] I am happy for maintainers to push small adjustments to this PR,
   - to speed up the review cycle
   - - [ ] I have checked that there are no existing pull requests for the
   - same thing
  * fix(config): preserve comments in `atuin config set` (#3766)
   - Currently, when `atuin config set` modifies an existing key, any comment
   - above that key is deleted:
   - Before:
   - ```toml
   - auto_sync = true
   - # some comment here
   - # another comment here
   - style = "auto"
   - ```
   - After `atuin config set style full`:
   - ```toml
   - auto_sync = true
   - style = "full"
   - ```
   - This PR fixes the issue by transferring the old decor from the existing
   - value.

